# How to cite EEGSourceFC (Citation File Format, https://citation-file-format.github.io;
# GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository").
# The references are the code this pipeline was built from and the toolboxes
# it calls; docs/references.md adds the methods.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EEGSourceFC, please cite it as below, together with the code
  it was built from and the toolboxes and methods of the parts you used
  (docs/references.md).
type: software
title: "EEGSourceFC: static EEG source connectivity and power spectra"
abstract: >-
  A MATLAB pipeline for resting-state EEG. From cleaned scalp recordings it
  estimates the activity of cortical regions (eLORETA, LCMV or wMNE on the
  ICBM152 template head), measures the connectivity between every pair of
  regions as the mean of short windows or over the whole recording (wPLI,
  orthogonalised AEC and other measures) and the power spectra of every channel and region, and compares
  groups or correlates with clinical scores on the edges (network-based
  statistic), the graph metrics, the network blocks and band power, with
  permutation statistics. It is the static part of EEGSourceStates.
authors:
  - family-names: "Aubonnet"
    given-names: "Romain"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5395-775X"
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Psychophysiology and Cognitive Neuroscience, Department of Systems Medicine, University of Rome Tor Vergata, Rome, Italy"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/AuRomain/EEGSourceFC"
keywords:
  - EEG
  - source connectivity
  - functional connectivity
  - power spectrum
  - network-based statistic
  - resting state
  - MATLAB
